finding: P1 src/extras/effect-stack/index.ts:312-315 is an unchanged ImageBindings consumer that still treats ChromaticAberration.colorLut (documented registerImage id at lines 26-27) as a layer in ImageBindings.images. warmImages now partitions and renumbers layers by band. A lone 1024px registered LUT has id 0 in images1024 layer 0, but this consumer samples the empty band-0 fallback. Registering a >512px image first and a small LUT second gives LUT id 1 but band-0 layer 0; this consumer creates an out-of-range layer-1 view, producing a GPU validation error. This breaks ordinary app code and is not covered by the changed sampling call or existing replacement-texture LUT tests. Resolve this consumer through the same authoritative band/layer mapping. Pixel differences in the eight glTF scenes also remain unqualified against rendered reference evidence: isolating resampling establishes cause, not improved fidelity; the registered three.js parity suite checks decoded data/registration rather than rendered pixels.
